#X text 445 93 Step locks. seqstep <step> <1/0> selects (or lets go of) the step being written \, seqrecord <1/0> is the lock mode \, and seqvalue is every value the performer gives the parameter. The value array holds -1 where a step has no lock. The second array is the per-step mask \, so seqstepon <step> <0/1> silences a lock without losing its value. seqlockclear forgets every lock and nothing else: seqreset belongs to the record/loop automation and leaves the locks alone. Writing a value to a step switches its mask back on.;
#X obj 60 306 s \$1-seq-lock-written;
